// A builtin's parameter is not an interface, so nothing here says what
// `by_x` should become. Information flows from the target interface to the
// callback and never back, so with no target there is nothing to check it
// against (docs/closures-decision.md, "Where the target is *not* known").
type Point { int x; int y; }
int by_x(Point a, Point b) { return a.x - b.x; }
print(by_x);
